--- task
id: s06
dataset: social
kind: delete edges selected through a neighbour's property
answer: fewest
composition: a write fed by a read: edition 2's `delete … where` reads only the edge's own row, so the long comments come back first and the client passes their slugs on

--- intent
Remove the likes that `$who` gave to comments longer than `$min_length` characters.

--- params
{"who": "ann", "min_length": 15}

--- edition2
query long_comments($min_length: I64) {
  match { $c: Comment  $c.length > $min_length }
  return { $c.slug }
}

--- edition2 bind long=1:c.slug
query unlike($who: String, $long: [String]) {
  delete LikesComment where @src = $who and @dst in $long
}

--- edition3
query unlike_long($who: String, $min_length: I64) {
  $p: Person { slug: $who }
  $p $k:likesComment $c
  $c.length > $min_length
  delete $k
}

--- check
query check() {
  match { $p: Person  $p likesComment $c }
  return { $p.slug, $c.slug }
}

--- expect unordered
columns: ["p.slug","c.slug"]
["ann","c1"]
["bob","c1"]
["cyd","c2"]
